research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-2185-1.4 Additive identity: fix $m$ and induct on $n$; at $n = 1$, $(m+1) \cdot 1_F = m \cdot 1_F + 1_F$ by the recursion, and if $(m+n) \cdot 1_F = m \cdot 1_F + n \cdot 1_F$ then $(m+n+1) \cdot 1_F = (m+n) \cdot 1_F + 1_F = m \cdot 1_F + n \cdot 1_F + 1_F = m \cdot 1_F + (n+1) \cdot 1_F$. [given, algebra]
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-2186-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-2187-2.1 Inductive step: $(n+1) \cdot 1_F = n \cdot 1_F + 1_F$ is a sum of two positives, by the hypothesis and $1_F > 0$, hence $(n+1) \cdot 1_F > 0$. [step 1.2, L1, L2]
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-2188-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-2189-2.2 Iterating 1.3, for $m < n$ one has $m \cdot 1_F < n \cdot 1_F$, so $n \mapsto n \cdot 1_F$ is strictly increasing and therefore injective on $\{1, 2, 3, \dots\}$. [step 1.3, L2]
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-2190-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-2191-2.3 Multiplicative identity: fix $m$ and induct on $n$; at $n = 1$, $(m \cdot 1) \cdot 1_F = m \cdot 1_F = (m \cdot 1_F)(1 \cdot 1_F)$, and the step $(m(n+1)) \cdot 1_F = (mn + m) \cdot 1_F = (mn) \cdot 1_F + m \cdot 1_F = (m \cdot 1_F)(n \cdot 1_F) + (m \cdot 1_F)(1_F) = (m \cdot 1_F)((n+1) \cdot 1_F)$ uses 1.4 and distributivity. [step 1.4, algebra]
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-2192-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-2193-3.1 By induction on 1.1, 1.2, 2.1, $n \cdot 1_F > 0$ for every $n \ge 1$; with the strict increase 2.2 and the identities 1.4, 2.3, every claim holds. [step 2.1, step 2.2, step 1.4, step 2.3, discharge-induction] ∎
