research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1618-4.1 The $p$-series at $p = 1$ diverges, since $1 > 1$ is false; so $\sum |a_j|$ diverges. [step 3.2, L6]
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1619-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1620-5.1 Thus $\sum a_j$ converges while $\sum |a_j|$ does not, so $\sum a_j$ converges conditionally and not absolutely, and the claim [A1] fails for this series. [step 3.1, step 4.1, A1, L9]
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1621-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1622-6.1 The claim is therefore false. What survives of it is only the converse implication, that an absolutely convergent series converges. [step 5.1, A1, L10] ∎
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1623-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1624-## Remarks
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1625-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1626-- **The witness is not exotic.** It is the first series a reader meets whose convergence depends on cancellation, and the failure is as large as it can be: the series of absolute values does not merely converge to a different number, it diverges to $+\infty$.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1627-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1628-- **Everything on this page turns on this example.** Because the class of conditionally convergent series is nonempty, [[thm-riemann-series-theorem]] has content, and [[cor-unconditional-iff-absolute-in-r]] separates two genuinely different properties rather than restating one. The same series, with its rearrangements, is developed on the companion page.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md-1629-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-alternating-harmonic-series.md:1630:- **The value of the sum is not asserted here.** The series is proved convergent and nothing more; the classical evaluation needs the logarithm, which is later in the reading order ([[rem-sums-proved-to-exist-but-not-evaluated]]).
