research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-1456-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-1457-
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-1458-**Given:** The alternating sequence $(\varepsilon_j)$ with index maps $e$ and $o$, the sequence $b_j = 1/\iota(j+1)$, and the partial sums $t_n = \sum_{j<n} \varepsilon_j b_j$ ([[def-series]]).
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-1459-
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-1460-[L1] The alternating sequence: $\varepsilon_0 = 1$, $\varepsilon_{j+1} = -\varepsilon_j$, $|\varepsilon_j| = 1$; $e_0 = 0$, $e_{j+1} = e_j + 2$, $o_0 = 1$, $o_{j+1} = o_j + 2$; $\varepsilon_{e_j} = 1$ and $\varepsilon_{o_j} = -1$ ([[lem-alternating-sequence]]).
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-1461-
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-1462-[L2] The canonical naturals are positive for $n \ge 1$ and strictly increasing; reciprocation reverses the order on the positives; and for every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $n \ge 1$ with $1/\iota(n) < \varepsilon$ ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]], [[cor-archimedean-reciprocal]]).
--
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2091-4.1 Fix $j$. For every $m \ge j$ one has $t_{e_j} \le t_{e_m}$, and $(t_{e_m})_m$ converges to $L$, so $t_{e_j} \le L$; symmetrically $t_{o_j} \ge L$. This is the first half of claim 2. [step 3.1, step 3.2, L3]
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2092-
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2093-5.1 Let $n \in \mathbb{N}$. If $n = e_j$ then $t_n = t_{e_j} \le L$ and $t_{n+1} = t_{e_j+1} = t_{o_j} \ge L$; if $n = o_j$ then $t_n = t_{o_j} \ge L$ and $t_{n+1} = t_{o_j+1} = t_{e_{j+1}} \le L$. Since every $n$ is of exactly one of these two forms, $L$ always lies between $t_n$ and $t_{n+1}$, which is the second half of claim 2. [step 1.3, step 4.1, L1]
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2094-
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2095-6.1 Consequently $|L - t_n| \le |t_{n+1} - t_n| = |\varepsilon_n b_n| = |\varepsilon_n|\,b_n = b_n$ for every $n$, using $b_n \ge 0$ and $|\varepsilon_n| = 1$; this is claim 3. [step 5.1, step 1.4, step 1.1, L1, L8] ∎
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2096-
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2097-## Remarks
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2098-
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2099-- **The two hypotheses are not interchangeable with "$b_k \to 0$" alone.** A null sequence that is not monotone can make $\sum \varepsilon_k b_k$ diverge, and the bracketing of step 3.1 is exactly where monotonicity enters; the error bound is false without it. The test as stated is the classical Leibniz criterion.
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2100-
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2101-- **Why the index maps rather than "$2j$" and "$2j+1$".** The even and odd index maps come from [[lem-alternating-sequence]] together with the parity object itself, and step 1.3 is the only arithmetic needed about them. Rebuilding $(-1)^k$ by a fresh recursion inside this proof, and then proving afresh that the even indices and the odd indices partition $\mathbb{N}$, is precisely what that lemma exists to prevent.
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md-2102-
research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/ex-abel-test-applied--8d249dd927834d2c.prompt.md:2103:- **What the test does not give.** It produces the sum $L$ as a limit and bounds the error, and it identifies $L$ with no closed expression. For the alternating harmonic series the value is not available at this point in the reading order; see [[rem-sums-proved-to-exist-but-not-evaluated]].
