research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-113-natural, that is a set, so it is not an element of $\mathbb{R}$ and cannot be
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-114-divided into $1$. The canonical natural $\iota(n) = n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$ is the
