research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-112-**A note on the notation $\iota$.** A natural number here is a von Neumann
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-113-natural, that is a set, so it is not an element of $\mathbb{R}$ and cannot be
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-114-divided into $1$. The canonical natural $\iota(n) = n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$ is the
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-115-real number that $n$ names ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]]), so $1/\iota(k+1)$ is
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-116-what an informal text writes as $1/(k+1)$; the shift by one is there because
--
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-197-limit, and says why a zero limit has to be excluded.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-198-[[thm-infinite-product-criterion]] carries the elementary theory: the Weierstrass
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-199-bounds $1 + \sum_{k<n} p_k \le \prod_{k<n}(1+p_k)$, with the companion upper bound
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-200-$\prod_{k<n}(1+p_k) \le 1/(1 - \sum_{k<n}p_k)$ whenever $\sum_{k<n} p_k < 1$, the
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-201-equivalence of $\prod(1+p_k)$ with $\sum p_k$ for nonnegative terms, the
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-202-$(1-p_k)$ form together with the fact that its partial products tend to $0$ when
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-203-$\sum p_k$ diverges, and convergence of $\prod(1+p_k)$ from convergence of
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-204-$\sum |p_k|$ for signed terms.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-205-[[fs-infinite-product-converges-iff-terms-tend-to-one]] records that factors
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-206-tending to $1$ decide nothing. **No logarithm is used anywhere on this page**;
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-207-every one of those inequalities is an induction on finite products, and the
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-208-refinement usually proved with logarithms is deferred, as
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log:209:[[rem-sums-proved-to-exist-but-not-evaluated]] records.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-210-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-211-**Decimal expansions.** [[thm-decimal-expansions]] is the payoff of the geometric
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-212-series in this direction: for an integer $b \ge 2$ every $x \in [0,1)$ is the sum
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-213-of $\sum_{j\ge0} \iota(d_j)/\beta^{\,j+1}$ for a digit sequence that is unique
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-214-once the sequences eventually constantly $b-1$ are excluded. The construction is
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-215-**floor-free**: the integer part of a real is developed later in the reading
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-216-order, so the digit at each stage is selected by a finite case distinction closed
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-217-by the well-ordering principle, and the digits are assembled by the recursion
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry2-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-218-theorem.
