research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry1-ex-alternating-harmonic-rearranged-to-three-halves.prompt.md-1595-**Given:** The alternating sequence $(\varepsilon_j)$ with index maps $e$ and $o$, the sequence $b_j = 1/\iota(j+1)$, and the partial sums $t_n = \sum_{j<n} \varepsilon_j b_j$ ([[def-series]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry1-ex-alternating-harmonic-rearranged-to-three-halves.prompt.md-1596-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry1-ex-alternating-harmonic-rearranged-to-three-halves.prompt.md-1597-[L1] The alternating sequence: $\varepsilon_0 = 1$, $\varepsilon_{j+1} = -\varepsilon_j$, $|\varepsilon_j| = 1$; $e_0 = 0$, $e_{j+1} = e_j + 2$, $o_0 = 1$, $o_{j+1} = o_j + 2$; $\varepsilon_{e_j} = 1$ and $\varepsilon_{o_j} = -1$ ([[lem-alternating-sequence]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry1-ex-alternating-harmonic-rearranged-to-three-halves.prompt.md-1598-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry1-ex-alternating-harmonic-rearranged-to-three-halves.prompt.md-1599-[L2] The canonical naturals are positive for $n \ge 1$ and strictly increasing; reciprocation reverses the order on the positives; and for every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $n \ge 1$ with $1/\iota(n) < \varepsilon$ ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]], [[cor-archimedean-reciprocal]]).
