research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry1-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-211-**Decimal expansions.** [[thm-decimal-expansions]] is the payoff of the geometric
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry1-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-212-series in this direction: for an integer $b \ge 2$ every $x \in [0,1)$ is the sum
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry1-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-213-of $\sum_{j\ge0} \iota(d_j)/\beta^{\,j+1}$ for a digit sequence that is unique
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry1-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-214-once the sequences eventually constantly $b-1$ are excluded. The construction is
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry1-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-215-**floor-free**: the integer part of a real is developed later in the reading
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry1-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-216-order, so the digit at each stage is selected by a finite case distinction closed
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry1-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-217-by the well-ordering principle, and the digits are assembled by the recursion
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-a6-retry1-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-218-theorem.
