items/def-complex-logarithms-principal-logarithm-and-complex-powers.md:29:The set of all complex logarithms of $z$ is
items/def-complex-logarithms-principal-logarithm-and-complex-powers.md:33:Thus the first is one specified complex number and the second is a set of complex numbers; neither notation silently identifies them. The conventions and prerequisite facts used below are recorded in [[thm-polar-form-with-unique-principal-argument]], [[def-natural-logarithm]], [[def-complex-exponential]], [[thm-complex-numbers-form-a-field]].
